WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:03.120
What is this?

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:05.250
"Pickled vegetables"...

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.170
Perhaps she means to thank us for letting her stay.

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:11.050
I will sample it, Sire.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:16.550
Well?

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.720
Quite good, for enemy food...

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:23.020
Why is there a key on the floor?

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:27.610
I'd say she opened the window before she locked the door outside,

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:29.610
then tossed the key through it.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.740
That's a hero for you. Exemplary conduct.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:35.410
What would you do?

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:37.120
That's obvious.

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:41.290
I would lock the door, then take the key with me.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:42.620
You're a demon.

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:44.750
Indeed. And?

00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:00.600
<i>Kono shunkan, kono basho ga sutaato</i>

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:06.650
<i>Imeeji shite miyou naniga dekiru no ka na</i>

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:10.610
<i>Shinjirarenai dekigoto datte aru</i>

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:16.320
<i>Motto... koete yukeru ne</i>

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:27.290
<i>Zero kara umareru subete kagayaite ano sora e</i>

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:31.760
<i>Omoikiri habatakitai</i>

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:38.890
<i>Saikou no sumairu de warainagara saa yukou!</i>

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:44.730
<i>Michi no sekai e to ima tobidasou yo</i>

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:49.400
<i>Mirai wo erabi, kimeru no wa jibun</i>

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:51.690
<i>Yume wo oikakete yukou</i>

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:53.320
<i>Naku hi mo aru</i>

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:59.620
<i>Sore wa daiji na negai, kienaide</i>

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:07.540
<i>Kitto aeru kara, asu no kimi e...</i>

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:28.850
I feel defiled.

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:34.730
Turning to our next story...

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:38.860
Shots were fired in a residential area of Shibuya before dawn this morning.

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:41.660
Several bullet marks have been found in nearby buildings,

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:45.290
and a bicycle hit with multiple shots was abandoned near the scene.

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:48.830
--Police believe it's related to the crime,

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:47.580
--Gah, those two!

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:48.830
--Idiots...

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:51.500
--Well, I guess it's not my problem.
--and are tracking down the owner now.

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:54.840
Police are investigating possible links to a recent string

00:02:55.050 --> 00:03:00.800
of late-night muggings and convenience store robberies in the neighborhood.

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:03.300
--Oh dear, that's almost our neighborhood!
--Moving on...

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:06.140
--Isn't that right near where you work, honey?
--There was an earthquake in the Kanto region

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:08.730
at approximately 6:20 this morning.

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:16.150
I'm not joking or imagining things.
I really think an earthquake is coming!

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:21.700
Um, if you don't mind, could I ask your advice about this in person?

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:25.620
Here goes!

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:29.830
Okay. Does tomorrow evening work?

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:34.130
I've got the day off, and you're not on shift either, right?

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:38.760
Chiho, are you working today?

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:44.850
Huh? Uh, no! Today I, um... have other stuff to do!

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:46.850
You be careful, now.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:49.770
A-A-A-About what?! What do you mean?!

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:51.980
This neighborhood's dangerous lately.

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:53.520
Oh, that.

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:55.270
What else would it be?

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:57.480
Nothing, never mind!

00:03:57.690 --> 00:03:58.650
Chiho!

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:03.820
Hey, Emi, don't you live close to where that shooting happened?

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:05.910
I'm three train stops from there!

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:09.160
Oh, huh. So, what are you doing for lunch?

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:12.170
Wanna finally go to that curry place?

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:14.210
I should warn you, there might be a line.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.630
Sorry, I don't have time to stand in line today.

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:19.010
I lost my wallet.

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:20.590
What? For real?!

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:24.470
Now I have to fill out a bunch of forms on my break.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:30.890
Thank you for your call. This is Emi Yusa.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:37.440
"Yusa"? Sounds like you're a regular
Japanese already... Emilia the Hero.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:39.400
May I ask who's calling?

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:42.070
Someone who knows about the hero and the Devil.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:46.490
Someone with a plot to destroy you both.

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:50.790
In which case, your repeated access attempts last night...

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.710
I certainly didn't expect you and the Devil to form a united front.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:57.840
I assure you that was not our company's desired result.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:04:59.380
I imagine not.

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:05.220
Either way, the extermination of
King Satan and Emilia the hero

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:07.680
is Ente Isla's collective will.

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:09.430
Excuse me?!

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:16.400
I-I'm afraid I won't have an answer until we investigate the situation.

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:19.480
The situation that the hero and the Devil fled from a little gunfire?

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:23.700
How do you plan to investigate that?
I'm quite interested.

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:28.530
This vile tone that seems to echo from the pits of darkness...

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:30.660
He's a demon.

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:34.830
Alciel is the only great general left alive.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:37.460
Who in the demon realm are you?

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:42.800
Perhaps you think you can scare me with the words "Ente Isla's will,"

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:46.130
but I don't listen to those from your realm.

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:49.470
I see. It's a shame you don't believe me.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:51.600
Talk to you again soon.

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:01.020
It takes all kinds, huh?

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:06.990
Let's do lunch first. I'm sure the banks are crowded right now anyway.

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:10.660
Hello?

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:14.910
Hello, have I reached the cell phone of Miss Emi Yusa?

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:17.080
Yes, that's right...

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:20.080
I'm calling from the Yoyogi Police Station.

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:21.790
Huh?

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.460
Police?!

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:33.260
I never thought they'd ID us from that bike...

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:35.220
Japanese police are pretty good.

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:40.400
Still, we were right about the hero fudging her age.

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:43.480
As I recall, she's really about seventeen or eighteen.

00:06:43.690 --> 00:06:49.360
Told you she must've registered as at least twenty.

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:51.950
Don't people usually fudge <i>downward</i>, though?

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:55.120
My question is, why is the expression "fudge"?

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:57.960
Who cares about that?!

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:02.460
Why... Why... Why do I...

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:08.930
Why do I, a <i>hero</i>, have to be the demons' guarantor?!

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:13.970
Wh-What were we supposed to do?
We couldn't think of anybody else.

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:18.270
It's not as though we wanted to ask for <i>your</i> help with a thing like this.

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:23.230
Well, <i>I</i> never thought I'd have to use my seal and ID card for this!

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:26.690
I guess I could've asked my boss, but...

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:28.690
We mustn't cause her trouble.

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:30.450
But it's okay to cause <i>me</i> trouble?!

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:34.830
Well, duh. Causing heroes trouble is the whole point of devils, right?

00:07:35.030 --> 00:07:37.910
Does that make choosing me logical?!

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:41.170
Aw, come on, we let you stay over last night.

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:44.420
Calm down, Emilia.
That's pathetic behavior in a hero.

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:47.460
I'm not takin' that from <i>you</i>, Alciel!

00:07:47.670 --> 00:07:51.550
Your fridge was empty! Put a little more thought into your grocery shopping!

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:54.850
"Most resourceful general in the demon army" my butt!

00:07:55.430 --> 00:07:59.480
But it's... it's not my fault...!

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:04.560
Listen up: I just got a threatening call at work.

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:08.190
And they're after you, too, King Satan.

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:09.610
What?

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:14.660
There, I warned you.
But <i>I'll</i> be the one to defeat you.

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:16.740
And don't you forget it!

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:20.290
Don't <i>you</i> forget we're in public.

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:27.840
A-Anyway! You just be careful not to get killed by some nobody before you're defeated by me!

00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:33.970
They're after me and her both?

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:37.100
And they called on the phone, of all things...

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:39.060
It's not my fault...

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:41.480
--Get a grip. It's time to go home.
--My budget is perfect...

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:44.480
I gotta meet Chi later.

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:46.310
I'm home!

00:08:57.990 --> 00:08:58.870
Okay!

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:01.750
Now, Sire,

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:06.210
where and when are you meeting
Miss Sasaki, and when will you be home?

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:08.630
What are you, my old lady?

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:11.550
We're meeting at five, at the east exit of Shinjuku Station.

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:15.180
We have some time, then.
All right, Sire, let us go.

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:16.970
Huh? Go where?

00:09:23.810 --> 00:09:26.150
Yes, this will do nicely.

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:29.610
Where did the money for this even come from?

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:33.900
Naturally I've prepared a secret stash for just this sort of emergency.

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:38.570
"Emergency"? All I'm gonna do is drink some tea, hear her out, and come home!

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:39.660
This isn't necess--

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:41.450
You jest!

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:47.000
A teenage girl never tells her true fears to anyone but close friends!

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:48.420
Not even her parents!

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:50.710
Yet she told you, Sire!

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:53.420
<i>Surely</i> you are wise enough to know what <i>that</i> means!

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:55.840
I-I know. Yes.

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:58.010
Not to mention...

00:09:58.220 --> 00:10:02.140
I cannot allow you to go on a date wearing Unislo from head to toe.

00:10:02.350 --> 00:10:04.350
Y-You little...

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:07.980
Apologize to the world's #1 apparel chain and to me for that!

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:20.570
Mr. Maou!

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:22.830
Hmm? Chi, is that a new haircut?

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:27.120
You noticed? I went for a shorter style! What do you think?!

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:28.750
Looks pretty good on you.

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:30.210
Score!

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:34.760
You look good, too. I thought maybe you only wore Unislo!

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:39.510
Oh, no, not that there's anything wrong with Unislo! Unislo is fine!

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:44.350
You just look... cooler than usual today.

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:47.440
Yeah, my roommate told me
I couldn't wear Unislo on dates.

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:50.270
Th-Then you think of this as a date?

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:52.480
Huh? Uh, I guess?

00:10:52.690 --> 00:10:53.690
Score!

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:54.860
So, what should we do?

00:10:55.070 --> 00:10:57.280
Let's go to Café Dotour!

00:10:57.490 --> 00:10:59.780
It's cheap, and it's pretty relaxing.

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:04.910
It's okay! Since you're giving me advice today, it's all my treat!

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:09.370
Hey, I'm an adult. I can treat you to that much, no prob.

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:10.790
So, shall we?

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.920
Um, M-Mr. Maou--

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:16.210
Um... well...

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:17.920
What? What's wrong?

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:20.800
Can I... hold your hand?

00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:23.510
That's all? Sure, I don't mind.

00:11:27.390 --> 00:11:28.480
--What's the matter?
--Hmm?

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:31.480
O-Oh, no, it's nothing!

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:32.940
Thank you!

00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:36.650
We'll get split up if we don't hold hands, anyway. It's super-crowded.

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:40.490
Definitely. Somehow I just knew.

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:52.120
What are you lurking here for?

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:54.710
Emilia!

00:11:54.920 --> 00:11:56.590
Don't use my real name!

00:11:56.800 --> 00:11:59.800
And more to the point, you're acting blatantly suspicious.

00:12:00.010 --> 00:12:02.260
Are you tailing someone?

00:12:02.470 --> 00:12:04.100
I-It's none of your business!

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:05.550
I'm a hero.

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:09.060
Do you think I'll just let it go when I catch you acting suspicious?

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:11.980
No, but please, just this once--for my sake.

00:12:12.190 --> 00:12:16.230
For <i>your</i> sake? I knew you when you were a demon.

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:17.360
Hey!

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:23.320
I'm so sorry, Sire!

00:12:23.530 --> 00:12:28.870
--Alci-- Ashiya! What are you planning to do to that girl, you scum?!

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:28.870
--You misunderstand!

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:31.790
His Majesty has no wicked intentions here!

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:34.540
Like a Devil can have <i>non</i>-wicked ones!

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:37.090
I'm begging you, listen to me!

00:12:39.170 --> 00:12:40.550
So that's how it is.

00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:42.340
So you understand now?

00:12:42.550 --> 00:12:47.640
My longtime foe is in a shameful state, I understand that much.

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:50.640
But why do they need to go on a date?

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:54.310
I wondered the same thing.
But after observing her,

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:58.520
it's clear that this "Sasaki" girl is more than a little fond of him.

00:12:58.730 --> 00:13:00.480
I imagine so.

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:02.450
That doesn't bother you at all?

00:13:02.650 --> 00:13:03.990
You want it to?

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:05.160
No...

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:08.330
I just feel it's insolent in the extreme

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:11.450
for a mere human girl to be enamored of my king...

00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:14.080
Personally, I wonder why a cute girl like that

00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:16.750
would be interested in a good-for-nothing like him.

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:18.670
You insult His Majesty?!

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:20.420
I <i>am</i> a hero.

00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:25.090
At any rate, right now any girl who took one look at her could tell.

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:30.600
That trendy summer dress, plus it looks like she was just at the salon.

00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:32.390
What's more, those are new shoes.

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:34.060
What? They are?

00:13:34.270 --> 00:13:36.980
Men can't tell these things, I suppose.

00:13:37.190 --> 00:13:39.730
She's using that material to evoke the freshness of early summer,

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:43.570
and the form-fitting cut to emphasize her curv-- Whoa, those are big.

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:44.280
What are?

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:48.740
N-Never you mind! It's not like big ones are useful in battle,

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:51.290
and small ones mean your plate armor is cheaper,

00:13:51.490 --> 00:13:53.290
and they don't get in the way, either!

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:55.920
--What are you talking about?
--Never you mind.

00:13:56.120 --> 00:13:59.880
Okay, so? Think you can get anything useful from her?

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:01.130
Don't ask me.

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:04.510
I'm just following them to check that no shady characters are around.

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:07.680
You're the shadiest one right now.

00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:12.520
Still, this earthquake thing bothers me.

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:16.890
If what's going on with her is connected to our world...

00:14:17.100 --> 00:14:20.650
There's no point in spying on them from here! Let's go.

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:21.940
Go where?

00:14:22.150 --> 00:14:24.650
That café, obviously!

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:25.440
What?!

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:28.990
How could I ever excuse such audacity to His--

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:32.700
Hey! <i>Stop</i>!

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:42.250
So, could you give me the details one more time?

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:46.760
All right. I told you that my tinnitus got really bad

00:14:46.970 --> 00:14:50.930
around the time I started working at MgRonald's, right?

00:14:51.140 --> 00:14:56.060
At first, I thought I was just tired from doing work I wasn't used to.

00:14:56.270 --> 00:14:58.020
But last night...

00:14:59.350 --> 00:15:01.940
Hello, can anybody hear me?

00:15:02.150 --> 00:15:04.070
Can anybody hear me?

00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:06.360
--Hello?
--Can anybody hear me?

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:10.740
--Hello!
--No good, huh. I guess they can't hear me.

00:15:10.950 --> 00:15:15.120
--I-I can hear you!
--Oh, well. Not too many people have the reception for it.

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:20.250
--What's going on?
--I'm sure disturbances are happening in your world right now.

00:15:20.460 --> 00:15:24.630
--A big one might be coming soon, so watch out.

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:24.630
--A "big one"?

00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:28.670
I'll come when the time is right.

00:15:30.010 --> 00:15:33.600
I could understand him even though
I'd never heard his language before.

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:35.350
I'm so confused...

00:15:35.560 --> 00:15:40.520
So you figured he must mean the quakes, since they're the main "disturbances" lately.

00:15:40.730 --> 00:15:42.190
Yes.

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:43.690
No doubt about it--

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:46.610
That was the communication method where humans in different worlds

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:50.820
tune their minds in to each other and share concepts... The idea link.

00:15:51.030 --> 00:15:53.950
They use sonar probe technology to do it.

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:59.910
When the sonar pulse reaches its target, it causes a magical explosion,

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:03.170
manifesting itself in various phenomena.

00:16:03.380 --> 00:16:08.960
It's perfectly possible that the pulses became earthquakes in this case.

00:16:09.170 --> 00:16:12.010
The fact that so many have happened near us makes sense

00:16:12.220 --> 00:16:18.350
if we posit that someone's using sonar to trace our and Emilia's route.

00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:21.640
A big one is coming soon, eh?

00:16:21.850 --> 00:16:25.270
Looks like things are gonna happen faster than I expected--

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:27.940
Are you okay?! What happened?!

00:16:28.150 --> 00:16:29.230
Why?

00:16:29.440 --> 00:16:32.030
Why is Emi walking into this café, and with Ashiya?!

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:33.360
Mr. Maou?

00:16:33.570 --> 00:16:36.200
It's okay. I'm not doing anything wrong!

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:37.410
Huh?

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:38.660
Sorry about that!

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:45.500
So, to summarize, the tinnitus and weird voices aren't really an issue.

00:16:45.710 --> 00:16:49.000
The important thing is whether a big one is really coming!

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:54.840
If so, I think just being able to warn the people around you will make a big difference!

00:16:55.050 --> 00:17:00.470
I'm so glad I asked you. It took some of the weight off my shoulders.

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:04.350
Hear that, Emi?! I'm not doing anything wrong!

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:07.820
Anyone can see I'm being the perfect senior part-timer!

00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:11.530
I couldn't tell my friends or my parents about it...

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:16.070
But I thought <i>you</i> might believe me, Mr. Maou.

00:17:16.280 --> 00:17:20.740
You're kind... And, um...

00:17:20.950 --> 00:17:25.790
M-Mr. Maou, um... I...

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:27.580
I-I like--

00:17:27.790 --> 00:17:29.590
Stop right there!

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:32.130
No good can come of associating with him.

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:33.720
E-Emi...!

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:36.510
This man isn't what he seems.

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:39.100
His true nature is cunning and cruel.

00:17:39.300 --> 00:17:42.640
D-D-D-Don't just pop out of nowhere and say mean things like that!

00:17:42.850 --> 00:17:46.230
Wh-Wh-What are you to him?!

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:50.690
I'm his enemy. Nothing more, nothing less.

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:53.110
Bad things will happen to you if you get involved with him.

00:17:53.320 --> 00:17:54.450
Hey, Emi, cut it out!

00:17:54.650 --> 00:17:56.660
Do not order me around.

00:17:56.860 --> 00:17:58.030
You calm down, too, Chi--

00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:01.080
You be quiet, Mr. Maou!

00:18:01.290 --> 00:18:05.250
Now I remember. You came to our restaurant the other day, didn't you?

00:18:05.460 --> 00:18:06.420
So what?

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:10.630
Are you his ex?

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:12.130
Where did <i>that</i> come from?!

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:14.260
Y-You <i>are</i>, then!

00:18:14.470 --> 00:18:20.220
In that case, however I come at him, it's none of your business anymore!

00:18:20.430 --> 00:18:24.770
Would you stop talking crazy?
We don't have that kind of relationship!

00:18:24.980 --> 00:18:28.560
Then why are you always hanging around him?

00:18:28.770 --> 00:18:32.650
What lies between us can't be explained in just a few words!

00:18:32.860 --> 00:18:35.990
Are you trying to say you're closer to him than I am?!

00:18:36.200 --> 00:18:37.780
Where did you get <i>that</i> interpretation?!

00:18:37.990 --> 00:18:39.910
It's the only possible interpretation!

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:42.990
Please, both of you, calm down...

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:49.960
--It's an earthquake!
--A huge one!

00:18:55.340 --> 00:18:56.470
Mr. Maou!

00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:02.390
What happened...?

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:05.180
Oh, good, you're awake.

00:19:05.390 --> 00:19:06.480
You're...

00:19:06.680 --> 00:19:10.600
Blech, we're completely trapped.

00:19:10.810 --> 00:19:12.190
Where's Mr. Maou?

00:19:12.400 --> 00:19:15.110
Not with us, I can tell you that much.

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:17.490
That's not what I...

00:19:17.690 --> 00:19:21.450
Oh, you're worried he got crushed by the rubble?

00:19:21.660 --> 00:19:27.370
True, he'd make a lot of people happy if he died today...

00:19:27.580 --> 00:19:30.210
But I guarantee he's alive.

00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:33.170
<i>I'll</i> be the one to defeat him.

00:19:33.380 --> 00:19:37.460
He's not allowed to die here!

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:42.800
Yes... I'm sure he's okay...

00:19:43.010 --> 00:19:45.930
Yep. He's okay.

00:19:46.140 --> 00:19:47.430
I'm Emi Yusa.

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:51.770
And FYI, there's really nothing between Maou and I, okay?

00:19:52.980 --> 00:19:57.230
I'm Chiho Sasaki.
I'll pretend to accept that for now.

00:19:57.440 --> 00:19:59.700
So, what made you fall for Maou?

00:19:59.900 --> 00:20:02.450
Wh-Wh-Wh-What are you talking about?!

00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:05.780
You picked a fight with me because you <i>like</i> him, right?

00:20:05.990 --> 00:20:09.580
L-L-Like?! No, I... I...

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:13.460
Am I that obvious?

00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:16.920
Anybody watching you could figure it out.

00:20:18.340 --> 00:20:22.930
M-Miss Yusa, how do you feel about Mr. Maou?

00:20:23.140 --> 00:20:24.300
Me?

00:20:24.510 --> 00:20:30.310
You seem really chummy with him, for someone who calls him her enemy.

00:20:30.520 --> 00:20:33.650
Boy, would I hate to be his chum...

00:20:33.850 --> 00:20:34.810
Huh?

00:20:35.020 --> 00:20:39.360
Well, it's true that we've known each other for a long time.

00:20:39.570 --> 00:20:43.530
But loving him will get you hurt.

00:20:43.740 --> 00:20:45.530
Don't say I didn't warn you, okay?

00:20:45.740 --> 00:20:48.040
I don't really understand...

00:20:48.240 --> 00:20:50.000
You will.

00:20:50.200 --> 00:20:53.870
Though actually, maybe it's better if you don't.

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:58.550
But for the moment... get a little sleep.

00:21:04.380 --> 00:21:08.470
You're close by, aren't you?
I've put Chiho to sleep!

00:21:10.850 --> 00:21:12.730
I don't need you butting in!

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:17.020
Maou?! What happened to your body?!

00:21:17.230 --> 00:21:20.110
Beats me. It just sorta changed.

00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:23.780
His magic is back?

00:21:23.990 --> 00:21:28.450
Man, I dunno how I'm supposed to explain this to anyone...

00:21:28.660 --> 00:21:30.830
Right now...

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:34.670
If I muster all the celestial force I have left <i>right now...</i>

00:21:34.870 --> 00:21:38.290
I can still make a sacred sword strong enough to defeat him!

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:40.170
Take care of Chi.

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:41.920
Time to get out of here.

00:21:42.130 --> 00:21:44.090
Looks like there are surprisingly few casualties,

00:21:44.300 --> 00:21:47.090
but we don't have time to wait around for rescue.

00:21:47.300 --> 00:21:49.260
I'll find us a way.

00:21:50.260 --> 00:21:52.140
You'll <i>find us a way</i>?

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:58.060
Okay, here we go...

00:21:58.270 --> 00:21:59.770
Why?

00:21:59.980 --> 00:22:04.490
Why... would the Devil <i>save</i> people?

00:22:23.210 --> 00:22:28.510
<i>Doko kara asa ni naru? Shizuka na sora</i>

00:22:28.720 --> 00:22:34.140
<i>Minai furi wo shita yubikiri koyubi no saki</i>

00:22:34.350 --> 00:22:44.350
<i>Warawareta tsuki nara kiete</i> <i>yuku n da kinou no houkaku e</i>

00:22:45.030 --> 00:22:50.280
<i>Usotsuki okubyoumono</i> <i>minna matomete boku nara</i>

00:22:50.490 --> 00:22:56.000
<i>Saite ita no wa yume no naka da</i>

00:22:56.200 --> 00:23:01.540
<i>Tsuki no kage ni kakushiteta</i> <i>hontou wa ne naiteta</i>

00:23:01.750 --> 00:23:07.260
<i>Namida wa mou nagarenai karete shimatta no?</i>

00:23:07.470 --> 00:23:13.810
<i>Nani mo ka mo yurusetara</i> <i>nagareru ka mo shirenai kedo</i>

00:23:14.010 --> 00:23:21.350
<i>Mamoritai mono bakari da na</i>
